# The partner repositories molpy is built against. scripts/partners.py
# resolves them, for every workflow (`partners.py fetch`) and for the git
# hooks (`partners.py run`) alike, so a local push is tested against the same
# partner commits as CI -- never against whatever the siblings ../molrs,
# ../mollog and ../molcfg happen to have checked out.
#
# KEY=VALUE lines only. SELF is this repository's directory in CI's sibling
# layout (molpy/, molrs/, mollog/, molcfg/).
#
# On dev, partners are tracked, not pinned: MOLRS_REF=dev is molrs's dev tip,
# and MOLLOG_REF / MOLCFG_REF=master are mollog's and molcfg's master tips
# (they have no dev) -- or each partner's branch of the same name as the one
# being built, when it has one (a change spanning repositories; see
# "Partners" in docs/developer/development-setup.md). pyproject.toml builds
# molcrafts-molrs, molcrafts-mollog and molcrafts-molcfg from those checkouts
# ([tool.uv.sources]). A release is tested against all three from PyPI instead
# (docs/developer/release-process.md).
#
# uv.lock records each partner's package metadata (its version and
# dependencies), not a commit. When a partner's tip changes that metadata,
# `uv lock --check` fails; relock in a commit of its own:
#   scripts/partners.py run -- sh -c 'uv lock && cp uv.lock "$PARTNERS_SOURCE/"'
SELF=molpy
MOLRS_REPOSITORY=MolCrafts/molrs
MOLRS_REF=dev
MOLLOG_REPOSITORY=MolCrafts/mollog
MOLLOG_REF=master
MOLCFG_REPOSITORY=MolCrafts/molcfg
MOLCFG_REF=master
